    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a favorable slate today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (77.01) and **Yordan Alvarez** (76.23). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, capitalizing on a significant dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) against Teng, while his leadoff spot provides the high-volume opportunities we prioritize in a 5x5 Roto format. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite a neutral matchup against Rea; his elite .419 xwOBA provides the floor necessary to hunt for HR and RBI, while **Christian Yelich** (75.84) rounds out our top-tier trio by exploiting a massive 19% boost from facing Sasaki\u2019s generous xERA of 5.11.\n\nWe are aggressively leveraging platoon edges and favorable order slots today. **Trea Turner** (69.64) is a core piece of our strategy, as he benefits from a slow opposing delivery that enhances his elite speed profile, helping us attack the scarcest category of the 5x5 landscape. While **Kyle Schwarber** (64.88) faces a wind risk\u2014a 5% deduction for \"Wind In\"\u2014his xwOBA of .401 keeps him safely in the \"Strong\" category. The most difficult bench decision was avoiding **Caleb Durbin**; despite a solid base projection of 52.35, he was omitted because he is not in the confirmed starting lineup. We continue to monitor the status of **Junior Caminero**, whose postponement leaves a hole in our utility depth, though the active roster remains well-positioned to maximize daily efficiency scores.",
